Sira: (This is my mandau pusaka.)
Sira: (A sacred blade forged from Batu Mantikei, a carved deer-antler as its hilt, and sheathed in kayu ulin.)
Sira: (This mandau has been passed down for generations.)
Sira: (It chose me as its next owner.)
Sira: (Even if I'm not spiritually sensitive like the Balian,)
Sira: (I can still feel the Tunggul housing this mandau.)
Sira: (Dad said the Tunggul is one of our ancestors who was a great warrior.)
Sira: (The mandau can fly on its own to protect its people and land.)
Sira: (I haven't been able to invoke it on my own yet.)
Sira: (It's forbidden to unsheathe the mandau without a reason after all.)
Sira: (I usually keep it in a special place inside the long house but it's outside because the Balian was using it for Manajah Antang)